1
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:02,300
In March twenty twenty four,

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:05,252
a man stood in front of reporters in Port

3
00:00:05,272 --> 00:00:08,204
au Prince and made a threat to an entire

4
00:00:08,224 --> 00:00:08,532
country.

5
00:00:09,852 --> 00:00:12,229
If the prime minister did not resign,

6
00:00:12,249 --> 00:00:15,312
he said, it would lead directly to a civil

7
00:00:15,332 --> 00:00:17,367
war, which would end in genocide.

8
00:00:17,387 --> 00:00:19,765
Weeks later, the prime minister was gone.

9
00:00:21,885 --> 00:00:24,662
The man was a former police officer.

10
00:00:24,682 --> 00:00:28,259
Today, the United States offers up to five million

11
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:31,056
dollars for information leading to his arrest.

12
00:00:31,076 --> 00:00:33,454
And the soldiers of El Salvador,

13
00:00:33,474 --> 00:00:35,052
the country of CECOT,

14
00:00:35,072 --> 00:00:38,249
are now hunting gang leaders in his city.

15
00:00:39,569 --> 00:00:42,351
His name is Jimmy Chérizier.

16
00:00:42,371 --> 00:00:45,713
Haiti knows him by another name.

17
00:00:45,733 --> 00:00:46,273
Barbecue.

18
00:00:49,013 --> 00:00:51,485
Chapter 1. Delmas.

19
00:00:56,085 --> 00:00:59,004
Jimmy Chérizier was born on March thirtieth,

20
00:00:59,024 --> 00:01:01,943
nineteen seventy seven, according to most sources,

21
00:01:01,963 --> 00:01:05,301
in Delmas, a district of Port au Prince,

22
00:01:05,321 --> 00:01:09,080
right next to the waterfront slum of La Saline.

23
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,526
He was one of eight children.

24
00:01:12,546 --> 00:01:15,031
His father died when he was five.

25
00:01:16,351 --> 00:01:19,716
His own explanation of his nickname is simple.

26
00:01:19,736 --> 00:01:21,409
His mother, he says,

27
00:01:21,429 --> 00:01:23,949
sold fried chicken on the street.

28
00:01:23,969 --> 00:01:26,911
Barbecue. His critics tell a different story.

29
00:01:26,931 --> 00:01:30,721
They say the name comes from people burned alive

30
00:01:30,741 --> 00:01:33,683
during attacks he is accused of leading.

31
00:01:33,703 --> 00:01:34,953
He denies it.

32
00:01:36,273 --> 00:01:39,272
That pattern, two completely different stories about the same

33
00:01:39,292 --> 00:01:42,291
man, would follow him for the rest of his

34
00:01:42,311 --> 00:01:42,627
life.

35
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:47,580
Chapter 2. The policeman.

36
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:55,234
Chérizier joined the Haitian National Police.

37
00:01:55,254 --> 00:01:58,821
He served in a unit called UDMO,

38
00:01:58,841 --> 00:02:02,407
used for crowd control and riot operations.

39
00:02:03,727 --> 00:02:06,849
In a country where police were poorly paid and

40
00:02:06,869 --> 00:02:09,642
badly equipped, and where gangs controlled whole neighborhoods,

41
00:02:09,662 --> 00:02:12,784
the line between officer and armed group was not

42
00:02:12,804 --> 00:02:13,483
always clear.

43
00:02:14,803 --> 00:02:18,811
In twenty seventeen, during a police operation in a

44
00:02:18,831 --> 00:02:20,602
neighborhood called Grand Ravine,

45
00:02:20,622 --> 00:02:23,287
at least nine people were killed.

46
00:02:23,307 --> 00:02:25,973
Chérizier was accused of being involved.

47
00:02:25,993 --> 00:02:28,659
It was not the last accusation.

48
00:02:30,799 --> 00:02:33,317
Chapter 3. La Saline.

49
00:02:37,917 --> 00:02:39,540
In November twenty eighteen,

50
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,595
armed men attacked La Saline,

51
00:02:41,615 --> 00:02:44,882
the neighborhood next to where he grew up.

52
00:02:44,902 --> 00:02:46,936
The violence lasted for days.

53
00:02:48,256 --> 00:02:51,100
How many people died is still disputed.

54
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:53,963
According to reporting by the Associated Press,

55
00:02:53,983 --> 00:02:57,644
a Haitian human rights network counted seventy one dead,

56
00:02:57,664 --> 00:03:01,326
while other witnesses spoke of at least twenty one

57
00:03:01,346 --> 00:03:05,007
men. Another local group put the toll at fifteen

58
00:03:05,027 --> 00:03:06,234
to twenty five.

59
00:03:07,554 --> 00:03:09,119
According to the U.S.

60
00:03:09,139 --> 00:03:12,290
Treasury, more than four hundred houses were destroyed,

61
00:03:12,310 --> 00:03:15,064
and at least seven women were raped.

62
00:03:16,384 --> 00:03:18,737
And according to the U.S.

63
00:03:18,757 --> 00:03:23,009
Treasury, Jimmy Chérizier, while still a serving police officer,

64
00:03:23,029 --> 00:03:25,857
planned and participated in the attack.

65
00:03:27,177 --> 00:03:28,954
He denies all of it.

66
00:03:28,974 --> 00:03:32,190
He has said he was somewhere else at the

67
00:03:32,210 --> 00:03:34,347
time. But in December twenty eighteen,

68
00:03:34,367 --> 00:03:35,785
the police fired him.

69
00:03:37,105 --> 00:03:39,620
The former officer did not disappear.

70
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:41,732
He went back to Delmas.

71
00:03:41,752 --> 00:03:43,844
And he built something bigger.

72
00:03:46,384 --> 00:03:48,995
Chapter 4. The G nine.

73
00:03:53,595 --> 00:03:55,325
In June twenty twenty,

74
00:03:55,345 --> 00:03:57,949
Chérizier released a video on YouTube.

75
00:03:57,969 --> 00:04:01,885
He announced an alliance of nine armed groups from

76
00:04:01,905 --> 00:04:05,821
across the capital. He called it the G nine.

77
00:04:05,841 --> 00:04:07,133
Family and allies.

78
00:04:08,453 --> 00:04:10,983
Within two years, according to the UN,

79
00:04:11,003 --> 00:04:14,260
the alliance had grown to more than a dozen

80
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,717
gangs. His own group,

81
00:04:15,737 --> 00:04:17,902
from Delmas, was at its core.

82
00:04:19,222 --> 00:04:23,352
The G nine was accused of something more troubling

83
00:04:23,372 --> 00:04:26,118
than crime. According to InSight Crime,

84
00:04:26,138 --> 00:04:30,268
it received weapons and police uniforms from the government

85
00:04:30,288 --> 00:04:32,112
of President Jovenel Moïse,

86
00:04:32,132 --> 00:04:34,879
even after Chérizier had been fired.

87
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:39,028
Critics alleged that the gangs were used to keep

88
00:04:39,048 --> 00:04:40,873
opposition neighborhoods in line.

89
00:04:40,893 --> 00:04:45,022
These are allegations. Moïse's party denied any alliance with

90
00:04:45,042 --> 00:04:45,945
the gangs.

91
00:04:47,265 --> 00:04:50,693
The killings continued. A Haitian human rights network,

92
00:04:50,713 --> 00:04:54,573
RNDDH, counted eighty one people killed in attacks on

93
00:04:54,593 --> 00:04:58,453
the Bel Air neighborhood between August twenty twenty and

94
00:04:58,473 --> 00:05:00,177
May twenty twenty one,

95
00:05:00,197 --> 00:05:01,902
and eighteen more missing.

96
00:05:01,922 --> 00:05:04,057
It blamed the G nine.

97
00:05:04,077 --> 00:05:06,213
The G nine denied it.

98
00:05:07,533 --> 00:05:09,347
In December twenty twenty,

99
00:05:09,367 --> 00:05:11,640
the United States sanctioned Chérizier.

100
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:14,392
It also sanctioned two government officials,

101
00:05:14,412 --> 00:05:18,520
Fednel Monchery, a former director at the Interior Ministry,

102
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:20,813
and Joseph Pierre Richard Duplan,

103
00:05:20,833 --> 00:05:24,940
a presidential delegate, accused of helping to supply weapons

104
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,234
for the La Saline attack.

105
00:05:28,554 --> 00:05:31,811
Chérizier began to talk less like a gangster,

106
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:33,859
and more like a politician.

107
00:05:33,879 --> 00:05:35,907
In June twenty twenty one,

108
00:05:35,927 --> 00:05:39,184
he announced what he called an armed revolution.

109
00:05:39,204 --> 00:05:41,232
The G nine, he said,

110
00:05:41,252 --> 00:05:43,690
would deliver Haiti from the opposition,

111
00:05:43,710 --> 00:05:46,148
the government, and the Haitian bourgeoisie.

112
00:05:47,468 --> 00:05:49,564
Weeks later, on July seventh,

113
00:05:49,584 --> 00:05:52,527
President Moïse was assassinated in his home.

114
00:05:52,547 --> 00:05:56,336
Chérizier appeared at the head of a crowd of

115
00:05:56,356 --> 00:05:58,453
more than a thousand people,

116
00:05:58,473 --> 00:06:00,992
demanding justice for the dead president.

117
00:06:02,312 --> 00:06:04,378
In May twenty twenty one,

118
00:06:04,398 --> 00:06:08,133
there were reports that Chérizier had been wounded in

119
00:06:08,153 --> 00:06:10,636
a gunfight with a rival group.

120
00:06:10,656 --> 00:06:13,556
He reappeared. He always seemed to reappear.

121
00:06:15,896 --> 00:06:18,344
Chapter 5. The fuel.

122
00:06:22,944 --> 00:06:25,010
In September twenty twenty two,

123
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:28,346
Chérizier showed how much power he really had.

124
00:06:29,666 --> 00:06:33,358
G nine fighters seized and blocked the Varreux fuel

125
00:06:33,378 --> 00:06:37,070
terminal, the main entry point for fuel into Port

126
00:06:37,090 --> 00:06:39,957
au Prince. According to the Associated Press,

127
00:06:39,977 --> 00:06:43,257
around ten million gallons of diesel and gasoline,

128
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:46,969
and more than eight hundred thousand gallons of kerosene,

129
00:06:46,989 --> 00:06:48,206
were trapped inside.

130
00:06:49,526 --> 00:06:52,019
Haiti ground to a halt.

131
00:06:52,039 --> 00:06:54,533
Gas stations closed. Schools closed.

132
00:06:54,553 --> 00:06:59,057
Hospitals cut services. In the middle of a cholera

133
00:06:59,077 --> 00:07:02,073
outbreak, the country could not move.

134
00:07:03,393 --> 00:07:07,105
His first demand was the resignation of the new

135
00:07:07,125 --> 00:07:08,764
prime minister, Ariel Henry.

136
00:07:08,784 --> 00:07:12,497
Later, according to a government official quoted by Haitian

137
00:07:12,517 --> 00:07:14,571
media, he asked for amnesty,

138
00:07:14,591 --> 00:07:17,474
and for government posts for his allies.

139
00:07:18,794 --> 00:07:20,898
In October twenty twenty two,

140
00:07:20,918 --> 00:07:24,721
the UN Security Council imposed its first sanctions on

141
00:07:24,741 --> 00:07:26,420
Haiti in five years.

142
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:29,819
His name was the first on the list.

143
00:07:29,839 --> 00:07:32,367
A travel ban, an asset freeze,

144
00:07:32,387 --> 00:07:34,067
and an arms embargo.

145
00:07:35,387 --> 00:07:37,205
In November, after negotiations,

146
00:07:37,225 --> 00:07:40,882
the blockade ended. He had made his point.

147
00:07:40,902 --> 00:07:44,100
Without him, the capital could not breathe.

148
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:49,436
Chapter 6. Live together.

149
00:07:54,036 --> 00:07:57,676
For years, Haiti's gangs had fought each other as

150
00:07:57,696 --> 00:07:59,302
much as the state.

151
00:07:59,322 --> 00:08:02,149
Chérizier's G nine and its rival alliance,

152
00:08:02,169 --> 00:08:05,808
G Pèp, had waged a bloody war over Cité

153
00:08:05,828 --> 00:08:08,655
Soleil. In July twenty twenty two alone,

154
00:08:08,675 --> 00:08:10,688
according to the Associated Press,

155
00:08:10,708 --> 00:08:14,347
at least fifty people were killed there in four

156
00:08:14,367 --> 00:08:14,754
days.

157
00:08:16,074 --> 00:08:17,900
On February twenty ninth,

158
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:22,055
twenty twenty four, Chérizier announced that they would now

159
00:08:22,075 --> 00:08:26,209
fight together. The new coalition was called Viv Ansanm.

160
00:08:26,229 --> 00:08:27,132
Live together.

161
00:08:28,452 --> 00:08:32,996
What followed was the collapse we described in our

162
00:08:33,016 --> 00:08:35,531
earlier video. Police stations attacked.

163
00:08:35,551 --> 00:08:40,094
The airport besieged. And on the night of March

164
00:08:40,114 --> 00:08:44,151
second, the two largest prisons in Haiti emptied.

165
00:08:44,171 --> 00:08:48,714
More than four thousand seven hundred prisoners walked out.

166
00:08:48,734 --> 00:08:50,235
Chérizier claimed responsibility.

167
00:08:51,555 --> 00:08:54,039
That was when he made his threat.

168
00:08:54,059 --> 00:08:56,185
If Henry did not step down,

169
00:08:56,205 --> 00:08:58,689
and the international community kept supporting him,

170
00:08:58,709 --> 00:09:00,835
it would lead to civil war,

171
00:09:00,855 --> 00:09:01,550
and genocide.

172
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:06,621
Henry, stuck abroad, announced his resignation on March eleventh.

173
00:09:06,641 --> 00:09:10,392
A gang leader had helped bring down a government.

174
00:09:12,312 --> 00:09:16,111
Chérizier told interviewers he was not interested in becoming

175
00:09:16,131 --> 00:09:19,930
president. He said he was fighting for the poor.

176
00:09:19,950 --> 00:09:22,476
His critics pointed to the bodies.

177
00:09:24,816 --> 00:09:27,264
Chapter 7. The foreigners.

178
00:09:31,864 --> 00:09:36,116
The international answer was a Kenyan led police mission,

179
00:09:36,136 --> 00:09:39,438
which arrived in June twenty twenty four.

180
00:09:39,458 --> 00:09:41,811
Chérizier mocked it. The Kenyans,

181
00:09:41,831 --> 00:09:46,082
he said, were protecting the interests of the American

182
00:09:46,102 --> 00:09:46,557
oligarchs.

183
00:09:47,877 --> 00:09:50,926
Later that year, he told the journalist Michael Deibert

184
00:09:50,946 --> 00:09:53,996
that the foreign force was a group of invaders,

185
00:09:54,016 --> 00:09:56,725
acting on the orders of the United States,

186
00:09:56,745 --> 00:09:57,748
Canada and France.

187
00:09:59,068 --> 00:10:02,395
The United States answered in its own way.

188
00:10:02,415 --> 00:10:04,486
In May twenty twenty five,

189
00:10:04,506 --> 00:10:07,832
it designated Viv Ansanm a foreign terrorist organization.

190
00:10:09,152 --> 00:10:11,502
In August twenty twenty five,

191
00:10:11,522 --> 00:10:15,768
the Justice Department unsealed an indictment against Chérizier and

192
00:10:15,788 --> 00:10:17,664
a naturalized American citizen,

193
00:10:17,684 --> 00:10:20,034
arrested weeks earlier in Pasadena,

194
00:10:20,054 --> 00:10:24,300
Texas, accused of sending him money in violation of

195
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:28,566
U.S. sanctions. The State Department offered up to five

196
00:10:28,586 --> 00:10:32,832
million dollars for information leading to his arrest or

197
00:10:32,852 --> 00:10:35,676
conviction. As the Justice Department noted,

198
00:10:35,696 --> 00:10:38,519
an indictment is merely an allegation.

199
00:10:39,839 --> 00:10:43,933
A U.S. prosecutor described him as a gang leader

200
00:10:43,953 --> 00:10:46,675
responsible for heinous human rights abuses,

201
00:10:46,695 --> 00:10:49,874
including violence against American citizens in Haiti.

202
00:10:52,214 --> 00:10:54,894
Chapter 8. The drones.

203
00:10:59,494 --> 00:11:02,404
Inside Haiti, the war had changed.

204
00:11:02,424 --> 00:11:04,845
The government began using drones.

205
00:11:06,165 --> 00:11:09,064
And the gangs kept fighting among themselves.

206
00:11:09,084 --> 00:11:12,817
On a single day in December twenty twenty five,

207
00:11:12,837 --> 00:11:14,903
according to the Associated Press,

208
00:11:14,923 --> 00:11:18,656
clashes between gangs killed at least forty nine people.

209
00:11:19,976 --> 00:11:22,259
In March twenty twenty five,

210
00:11:22,279 --> 00:11:26,406
security forces launched a large operation in lower Delmas,

211
00:11:26,426 --> 00:11:29,631
his stronghold, using drones and special units.

212
00:11:29,651 --> 00:11:32,856
Rumors spread that he had been wounded.

213
00:11:32,876 --> 00:11:34,238
He denied it.

214
00:11:35,558 --> 00:11:38,703
On January fourteenth, twenty twenty six,

215
00:11:38,723 --> 00:11:43,451
according to Reuters, an operation using small attack drones

216
00:11:43,471 --> 00:11:46,089
destroyed three of his homes.

217
00:11:46,109 --> 00:11:47,144
Chérizier survived.

218
00:11:48,464 --> 00:11:51,188
For a man who had built his power on

219
00:11:51,208 --> 00:11:53,932
controlling the ground, the threat now came from the

220
00:11:53,952 --> 00:11:54,237
sky.

221
00:11:56,577 --> 00:12:00,163
Chapter 9. Bukele's soldiers.

222
00:12:04,763 --> 00:12:07,701
And then, in October twenty twenty six,

223
00:12:07,721 --> 00:12:09,391
a new force arrived.

224
00:12:09,411 --> 00:12:13,194
After four Salvadoran technicians were ambushed and kidnapped in

225
00:12:13,214 --> 00:12:16,997
Croix des Bouquets, President Nayib Bukele promised to finish

226
00:12:17,017 --> 00:12:20,377
the gangs if they were not returned alive.

227
00:12:21,697 --> 00:12:25,339
By November, around two thousand to two thousand five

228
00:12:25,359 --> 00:12:29,001
hundred Salvadoran soldiers were reported to be in Haiti.

229
00:12:29,021 --> 00:12:31,442
They moved fast. According to reports,

230
00:12:31,462 --> 00:12:35,104
a gang leader from the Boston gang was killed

231
00:12:35,124 --> 00:12:36,732
by a loitering munition.

232
00:12:36,752 --> 00:12:38,766
The house of Wilson Joseph,

233
00:12:38,786 --> 00:12:40,800
leader of four hundred Mawozo,

234
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:42,835
was destroyed in a strike,

235
00:12:42,855 --> 00:12:46,497
after Bukele asked people online to help locate it.

236
00:12:47,817 --> 00:12:51,271
By mid November, according to the conflict monitor ACLED,

237
00:12:51,291 --> 00:12:54,745
more than one hundred people had been killed in

238
00:12:54,765 --> 00:12:55,517
the operations.

239
00:12:56,837 --> 00:12:58,779
As of our latest check,

240
00:12:58,799 --> 00:13:02,309
we found no reports of Salvadoran strikes directly targeting

241
00:13:02,329 --> 00:13:04,271
Chérizier or the G nine.

242
00:13:04,291 --> 00:13:07,801
But the message to every gang leader in Port

243
00:13:07,821 --> 00:13:09,763
au Prince was the same.

244
00:13:09,783 --> 00:13:11,332
The rules had changed.

245
00:13:13,652 --> 00:13:17,660
Some gang leaders said they would fight to the

246
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:21,687
end. The leader of four hundred Mawozo called for

247
00:13:21,707 --> 00:13:25,268
UN mediated talks. El Salvador rejected the idea.

248
00:13:26,808 --> 00:13:30,684
Chapter 10. Revolutionary or warlord?

249
00:13:35,284 --> 00:13:37,435
So who is Jimmy Chérizier?

250
00:13:38,755 --> 00:13:40,562
In his own words,

251
00:13:40,582 --> 00:13:44,673
a revolutionary. A defender of poor neighborhoods against politicians

252
00:13:44,693 --> 00:13:48,783
and the rich. A man who says he never

253
00:13:48,803 --> 00:13:49,697
massacred anyone.

254
00:13:51,017 --> 00:13:52,898
According to the United States,

255
00:13:52,918 --> 00:13:55,939
the United Nations, and Haitian human rights groups,

256
00:13:55,959 --> 00:13:59,360
the leader of a criminal coalition accused of mass

257
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:02,781
killings, extortion, and the collapse of a capital city.

258
00:14:04,101 --> 00:14:05,764
As far as we know,

259
00:14:05,784 --> 00:14:07,446
he has never been tried,

260
00:14:07,466 --> 00:14:08,792
and never been arrested.

261
00:14:08,812 --> 00:14:10,475
As of our latest check,

262
00:14:10,495 --> 00:14:13,167
he is still believed to be in Haiti.

263
00:14:15,287 --> 00:14:18,514
Now he faces the same force that turned El

264
00:14:18,534 --> 00:14:21,762
Salvador's gangs into rows of shaved heads in CECOT.

265
00:14:21,782 --> 00:14:24,288
Will Barbecue end up in a cell,

266
00:14:24,308 --> 00:14:27,174
